Here's how to handle each scenario in MSTest:

## 1. Windows-only tests (platform filtering)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("WindowsOnly")]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows registry.");

    // ... registry code
}
```

Or with a condition attribute (MSTest 3.x+):

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue() { /* ... */ }
```

## 2. Skip in CI (environment-based)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGPU")]
public void Render_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI — requires local GPU.");

    // ... GPU test
}
```

Then in CI you can also filter by category:
```bash
dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=RequiresGPU"
```

## 3. Flaky external API (retry pattern)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // MSTest 3.8+ built-in retry
public void Weather_ReturnsForecast()
{
    var result = _weatherClient.GetForecast("Seattle");
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

If you're on an older MSTest without `[Retry]`, use a helper:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void Weather_ReturnsForecast()
{
    RetryHelper.Execute(maxAttempts: 3, delay: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2), () =>
    {
        var result = _weatherClient.GetForecast("Seattle");
        Assert.IsNotNull(result);
    });
}
```

## 4. Cleanup even on failure (use `TestCleanup` or `try/finally`)

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string _tempFile;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Always runs, even if the test fails
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile, "test data");
        var result = MyProcessor.Process(_tempFile);
        Assert.AreEqual("expected", result);
    }
}
```

`[TestCleanup]` is the MSTest equivalent of a `finally` block — it runs after every test method regardless of pass/fail. For one-off cases, `try/finally` inside the test works too.

---

**Summary of attributes:**

| Scenario | Approach |
|----------|----------|
| Platform gate | `Assert.Inconclusive()` or `[OSCondition]` |
| CI skip | Env-var check + `TestCategory` filtering |
| Flaky retry | `[Retry(n)]` (MSTest 3.8+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` method |
